{"series": "pandas", "style": "terracotta", "layout": "grid", "cover_alt": {"badge": "12 lines", "kicker": "pandas cheat sheet", "sub": "Load, clean, analyse, combine. Copy, run, done.", "title": "Stop Googling<br>these 12 ~pandas~<br>lines."}, "slides": [{"type": "cover", "art": "python", "badge": "12 lines", "kicker": "pandas cheat sheet", "sub": "Load, clean, analyse, combine. The lines you'll type in every analysis.", "title": "12 pandas lines<br>you'll use in<br>~every~ project"}, {"type": "list", "lang": "python", "tag": "01-03 \u00b7 Load & inspect", "title": "First, ~look~ at the data.", "items": [{"n": 1, "h": "Read a CSV", "b": "Swap for read_excel() on .xlsx files.", "code": "df = pd.read_csv(\"sales.csv\")"}, {"n": 2, "h": "Get the full picture", "b": "Rows, columns, data types and non-null counts.", "code": "df.info()"}, {"n": 3, "h": "Count blanks per column", "b": "Run this before any analysis.", "code": "df.isna().sum()"}]}, {"type": "list", "lang": "python", "tag": "04-06 \u00b7 Clean", "title": "Then ~clean~ it.", "items": [{"n": 4, "h": "Remove duplicate rows", "b": "Add subset= to check only some columns.", "code": "df = df.drop_duplicates()"}, {"n": 5, "h": "Fill the blanks", "b": "Never leave NaN in a column you group by.", "code": "df[\"city\"] = df[\"city\"].fillna(\"Unknown\")"}, {"n": 6, "h": "Fix date columns", "b": "Now .dt.month and .dt.year work.", "code": "df[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"date\"])"}]}, {"type": "list", "lang": "python", "tag": "07-09 \u00b7 Analyse", "title": "Now ask ~questions~.", "items": [{"n": 7, "h": "Filter with two conditions", "b": "Use & and |, with brackets around each.", "code": "df[(df[\"sales\"] > 5000) &\n   (df[\"region\"] == \"North\")]"}, {"n": 8, "h": "Total by group", "b": "Same as a SUMIF across every region.", "code": "df.groupby(\"region\")[\"sales\"].sum()"}, {"n": 9, "h": "Top 5 rows", "b": "Faster to read than sort + head.", "code": "df.nlargest(5, \"sales\")"}]}, {"type": "list", "lang": "python", "tag": "10-12 \u00b7 Combine & reshape", "title": "Excel tricks, ~in pandas~.", "items": [{"n": 10, "h": "Frequency of each value", "b": "Your COUNTIF for every value at once.", "code": "df[\"city\"].value_counts()"}, {"n": 11, "h": "VLOOKUP another table", "b": "how=\"left\" keeps every row of df.", "code": "df.merge(products,\n  on=\"product_id\", how=\"left\")"}, {"n": 12, "h": "Pivot table", "b": "One line. Rows, columns, values, sum.", "code": "df.pivot_table(index=\"region\",\n  columns=\"month\", values=\"sales\",\n  aggfunc=\"sum\")"}]}, {"type": "table", "title": "Excel \u2192 ~pandas~", "cols": ["In Excel", "In pandas"], "hi": 1, "rows": [["VLOOKUP", "merge()"], ["Pivot table", "pivot_table()"], ["SUMIF", "groupby().sum()"], ["COUNTIF", "value_counts()"], ["Remove duplicates", "drop_duplicates()"], ["Filter", "df[condition]"]], "note": "Already know Excel? You already know **what** to do. pandas is just **how**."}, {"type": "cta", "title": "Save it.<br>Open ~Jupyter~.", "body": "Comment PANDAS and I'll DM you all 12 lines as a PDF.", "keyword": "PANDAS", "action": "Follow @thedataguy16"}]}